Yes, one would be just plain black. I corrected myself on the other 
subthread so I thought it would be clear here as well: I meant "not 
reflecting _and_ not absorbing/refracting, etc", i.e. leaving the rays 
alone and letting them go through, like a magicians basket seems to let 
épées through.

If the function of this block is symmetic, this would also mean that our 
emissions would not be detectable outside as well: they'll not reflect, 
but go throughout the universe in a state unvisible to the eye. One 
might imagine this as a membrane which transfers the waves to other 
dimensions and transfers then back again when hit a second time.

In this case if this block applies to the whole spectrum a magical 
heating system might be needed, since we won't be able to heat ourselves 
from the outside.

There would be inconsistencies with nethack in this case though:

* with this one WILL be able to see himself when invisible. When one is 
looking at oneself the eyes and the object, say one's arm, are at the 
two sides of a hole in a non-convex shape, meaning that the visible rays 
will pass through the arm's block and be converted back to visible 
within the block which surrounds the head!

* one would be able to see invisible upon gaining invisibility.

* one would not be able to see visible creatures oneself: if the rays 
are left to propagate untouched, there is no way that they can be 
detected by the eyes' receptors.

This proves that however we regard the field, as a block or not, it must 
not be symmetrical. And it must generate energy itself, whether for 
heating or for cloning the waves so that we can see them as well as 
letting them through.

